foreign  it's definitely been a rocky ride we've  seen so many ups and downs since the  pandemic the rise in crime  and the houseless and homeless  population  that continues to be a challenge that I  think the city is starting to get their  arms wrapped around so that's very  encouraging safety is a priority for  everyone and I think a lot of  the surrounding areas the residents that  live in the surrounding areas to  downtown still feel unsafe to come  downtown  you know certainly a different climate  than you know two years ago when we were  experiencing doing business during  pandemic and riots and everything else  that was going on there are no more  riots  um  but people still feel unsafe because  there's been a narrative that's been set  and I think as small business owners we  are going above and beyond running our  own businesses to come together as a  community create wonderful experience  encourage people to come back to  downtown and to feel safe but I think  the city needs to partner with us to do  that to ensure that it's not just a  one-sided effort  I think there's a lot more the city can  do the professional criminals that are  out there busting into businesses and  wreaking havoc truly we need to catch  those folks and we do need to prosecute  those folks I recognize there's a lot of  complications around our D.A but but  really not having enough public  defenders to defend these criminals but  when somebody has been recorded on  camera well over a dozen times backing  their vehicle into a business I think  it's time we do something about that I  want to be really clear there are  opportunist criminals that are out there  people that should not be confused with  our houseless population that are live  that are dealing with a lot of other  concerns drug addiction mental health  needs that people that really need  Services we'd like to see our police  work in concert with the DA's office and  work together and we'd like to see  police showing up in a timely manner to  these calls and these break-ins we'd  like to see a greater police presence I  think a greater presence of security  detail and not necessarily police  because they certainly have their hands  full and have serious crimes to deal  with but I remember when I moved here  from Los Angeles many years ago I was  always impressed that every once in a  while you would see an officer on on  horseback riding through the city and I  haven't seen that in some years and I  remember my kids really like being  amazed and thinking that was great so  something light-hearted like that I know  we have some bike Patrol now so more of  that where it's more friendly a friendly  presence but nevertheless a presence  that says there's safety there's  security if something should go awry but  I keep hearing we don't have enough  police out on the street if that truly  is the case then we need to enlist  others and we have Portland Bureau of  Transportation  let's get let's get them out there with  big lights on the sides of their  vehicles and let's get them driving  around we made a recommendation well  over a year ago that we have patrols  that are out shining shining lights on  buildings  a lot of it is just preventative you  know just keeping the eyes on these  businesses and keeping them from getting  repeatedly broken into

